Description: use the real aspect ratio of the window and check SDL init
 The 04 patch kept a 4:3 viewport after a resize while the shaders still
 used the fixed S_WIDTH/S_HEIGHT ratio (16:10), so the picture was
 distorted after a resize or a switch to fullscreen. The shaders build
 their projection from uniforms[10], so the whole drawable is now used
 and this uniform follows its real ratio (SDL_WINDOWEVENT_SIZE_CHANGED,
 which is also sent on fullscreen toggle, and SDL_GL_GetDrawableSize).
 Also call SDL_Init and stop with a message instead of crashing when the
 window or the OpenGL context cannot be created.
Author: Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>
Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-14
